  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -

capability mqtt/packets  every control packet written and read as a value, exactly as the standard lays it out
  heroes  mqtt.encode, mqtt.decode, mqtt.Packet
  go      packets (paho.mqtt.golang's and paho.golang's: ConnectPacket, PublishPacket, ..., ReadPacket, NewControlPacket, ControlPacket.Write)
  rust    mqttbytes::v4::Packet, mqttbytes::v5::Packet, Codec, check, mqttbytes::FixedHeader, PacketType, mqttbytes::qos, mqttbytes::Protocol, mqttbytes::Error, and each packet's record (ConnAck, Connect, Disconnect, PingReq, PingResp, PubAck, PubComp, PubRec, PubRel, Publish, SubAck, Subscribe, UnsubAck, Unsubscribe, Auth)
  python  -
  note    paho.golang v0.23.0 writes AUTH with its reserved flag set (the first byte 241); the standard asks 240 (MQTT 5.0 § 3.15.1), which `encode` writes and `decode` asks

capability mqtt/simple  one message published, or one read, in one call
  heroes  mqtt.connect, mqtt.publish, mqtt.next_message, mqtt.close
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  paho.mqtt.publish.single, paho.mqtt.publish.multiple, paho.mqtt.subscribe.simple, paho.mqtt.subscribe.callback
  note    three calls in the program; a module of its own for them would be a second way to do what these do

