  python  enable_bridge_mode

dropped
  go      Logger, NOOPLogger, ERROR, CRITICAL, WARN, DEBUG (logging; a failure here is a value), ConnectionLostHandler, DefaultConnectionLostHandler, OnConnectHandler, ConnectionAttemptHandler, ConnectionNotificationHandler and every ConnectionNotification type, ClientOptions.SetConnectionLostHandler, ClientOptions.SetOnConnectHandler, ClientOptions.SetConnectionAttemptHandler, ClientOptions.SetConnectionNotificationHandler, ClientOptions.SetReconnectingHandler (callbacks, which need a closure), ClientOptions.SetCustomOpenConnectionFn, OpenConnectionFunc, ClientOptions.SetDialer, ProxyFunction (a connection made by the program's own function), Client.OptionsReader and every ClientOptionsReader getter (the options are a record the program reads), DummyToken, PlaceHolderToken, PacketAndToken, TokenErrorSetter, MId
  rust    Request, ClientError, ConnectionError, OptionError, StateError, Outgoing (the plumbing of a channel between the client and its event loop), MqttOptions::request_modifier, MqttOptions::set_request_modifier (a function rewriting the WebSocket's request), Transport::Unix (no Unix socket in `net`)
  python  CallbackAPIVersion and every Callback* type, on_connect, on_connect_fail, on_disconnect, on_log, on_pre_connect, on_publish, on_subscribe, on_unsubscribe, connect_callback, connect_fail_callback, disconnect_callback, log_callback, pre_connect_callback, publish_callback, subscribe_callback, unsubscribe_callback, socket_open_callback, socket_close_callback, socket_register_write_callback, socket_unregister_write_callback, message_callback, user_data_get, user_data_set (callbacks and their context), enable_logger, disable_logger, logger, LogLevel, reinitialise, drop_out_messages, MessageState, MessageType, PahoClientMode, ConnectFlags, HTTPHeader, WebSocketHeaders, PayloadType, MQTTException, MalformedPacket
